### 1.5 ID strategy

**KEEP surviving IDs. Do NOT renumber.** Format ids are stored as raw `uint8` in `.quant`
checkpoints with no version tag, so renumbering would silently reinterpret existing files.

- `FORMAT_ID_SLOTS = 105` (the id space never shrinks)
- `FORMAT_COUNT = 60` (the number of live formats)
- `format_is_valid(Format)` — the single truth; replaces every range predicate
  (`format_is_base/k/grp/half/mx`) and every `wire_fmt < FORMAT_COUNT` clamp.

**Persistence compatibility:** the retired formats' *wire layouts* changed during the rewire,
so their payloads are not decodable by the new codecs. Old `.quant` files therefore carry a
header version and are **rejected by the new reader with an explicit message** (re-quantize
from the source model) rather than silently misdecoded. The one exception — the plain `_K_L`
rows, whose layout was byte-identical to their plain base — is remapped on read via
`legacy_format_id_remap()`.

