## 4. Industrial parity (NEW-1)

Every row must reach **≥ the reference PSNR at ≤ the reference BPW**. Reference implementations
live in `bench/bench_format_comparison.cpp` and must be faithful to the published specs.

| Our format | BPW | Reference to beat |
|---|---|---|
| `Q_16` | 16.00 | IEEE FP16 (lossless-ish) |
| `Q_8` | 8.00 | INT8 uniform (8.125), GGUF Q8_0 (8.5) |
| `Q_G_6` / `Q_6` | 6.00–6.50 | GGUF Q6_K (6.5625) |
| `Q_G_4` / `Q_4` | 4.00–4.50 | GGUF Q4_K (4.5), AWQ 4-bit, GPTQ 4-bit |
| `Q_1_K_H` | 1.50 | **BitNet b1.58** (1.58) — must win at a LOWER bpw |
| `Q_1` / `Q_G_1` | 1.00 | Binary 1-bit |
| `Q_G_8` / `Q_8` | 8.00–8.50 | MXFP8 (8.0) |
| `Q_G_4` | 4.00–4.50 | MXFP4 (4.0) |
| `Q_G_6` | 6.00–6.50 | MXFP6 (6.0) |
| `Q_G_2` / `Q_2` | 2.00–2.50 | MXFP2, FP4-style |

**Fidelity fix owed:** the bench's `rt_gguf_q6k` reference uses per-16 int8 scales and drops the
global FP16 `d` (`(void)d;`) — it is NOT the published Q6_K scheme (whose 210 B/256-block layout
is 192 B levels + 16 B int8 scales + 2 B fp16 d). It must be made faithful before any
"we beat Q6_K" claim is allowed.

**New references to implement:** MXFP4/MXFP6/MXFP8 (block-scaled microscaling), AWQ 4-bit,
GPTQ 4-bit — all labelled `[ref]` and quarantined from the production codec.

